  "name": "redux-rs",
  "description": "A high-performance Redux state container implementation for Rust, leveraging nanosecond-precision timestamps for unique action identification and deterministic ordering. It provides a robust framework for state management through pure reducers, side-effect orchestration, and enabling conditions that validate actions against current state. The architecture includes specialized support for hierarchical state composition via sub-stores and distributed callback serialization for complex cross-thread or cross-platform execution.",
